  "description": "Implement autoregressive scaled dot-product attention with an upper-triangular causal mask preventing future token lookahead.\n\nCausal masking enforces temporal order during transformer decoding, preventing representations from leaking future target tokens.\n\n### Mathematical Formulation\n$$\n\\operatorname{Attention}(Q, K, V) = \\operatorname{softmax}\\left( \\frac{Q K^T}{\\sqrt{d_k}} + M \\right) V, \\quad M_{ij} = \\begin{cases} 0 & j \\le i \\\\ -\\infty & j > i \\end{cases}\n$$\n\n### Step-by-Step Implementation\n1. Compute raw attention logits via scaled matrix dot-product Q K^T / sqrt(d_k)\n2. Add upper-triangular causal attention mask with negative infinity penalties\n3. Compute normalized softmax attention weights and project over values V\n\n### Returns\nDictionary with 'output' tensor and 'attention_weights' matrix.",
  "theory": "## Understanding the Theory: Masked Causal Attention\n\n### Core Intuition: Why Do We Need This?\nNatural language consists of discrete words and symbols arranged in sequential order. To process text with neural networks, we convert words into continuous embedding vectors and model their grammatical and semantic relationships. **Masked Causal Attention** is a core sequence-processing mechanism used in modern Transformer and LLM architectures.\n\nCausal masking enforces temporal order during transformer decoding, preventing representations from leaking future target tokens. In this problem, the goal is to: implement autoregressive scaled dot-product attention with an upper-triangular causal mask preventing future token lookahead.\n\n### Mathematical Principles & Formulation\nThe core governing equation for this operation is:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{Attention}(Q, K, V) = \\operatorname{softmax}\\left( \\frac{Q K^T}{\\sqrt{d_k}} + M \\right) V, \\quad M_{ij} = \\begin{cases} 0 & j \\le i \\\\ -\\infty & j > i \\end{cases}\n$$\n\nEvery term in this formulation plays a precise mathematical role in ensuring dimensional consistency, numerical stability, and correct algorithmic behavior.\n\n### Step-by-Step Computational Workflow\n1. **Phase 1**: Compute raw attention logits via scaled matrix dot-product Q K^T / sqrt(d_k)\n2. **Phase 2**: Add upper-triangular causal attention mask with negative infinity penalties\n3. **Phase 3**: Compute normalized softmax attention weights and project over values V\n\n### Practical Machine Learning Applications & Nuances\n* **Self-Attention Mechanics**: Scaled dot-product attention computes all-to-all token interactions dynamically, allowing tokens to gather context from the entire sentence simultaneously.\n* **Position Encodings**: Because self-attention is permutation-invariant, positional encodings (like sinusoidal or Rotary Position Embeddings) inject word order into the representations.\n* **Vocabulary & Subwords**: Algorithms like BPE tokenize text into frequent subwords, allowing models to represent rare words without requiring an infinite vocabulary.",
