  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Masked Causal Attention** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport torch, math, numpy as np\n\ndef pytorch_masked_causal_attention(q: list, k: list, v: list) -> dict:\n    Q, K, V = torch.tensor(q, dtype=torch.float32), torch.tensor(k, dtype=torch.float32), torch.tensor(v, dtype=torch.float32)\n    D, S = Q.shape[-1], Q.shape[-2]\n    scores = torch.matmul(Q, K.transpose(-2, -1)) / math.sqrt(D)\n    i = torch.arange(S).unsqueeze(1)\n    j = torch.arange(S).unsqueeze(0)\n    mask = torch.where(j > i, float('-inf'), 0.0)\n    weights = torch.softmax(scores + mask, dim=-1)\n    out = torch.matmul(weights, V)\n    return {'output': np.round(out.numpy(), 4).tolist(), 'attention_weights': np.round(weights.numpy(), 4).tolist()}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
